---
description: Security rules for the sample todo app
alwaysApply: true
---

- Never write, log, or echo secrets, API keys, or production credentials in any file
- No `eval` on user input under any circumstances
- No `html_safe` or `raw` on untrusted or user-supplied input
- Use parameterized queries only — never string-interpolate values into SQL
- Do not disable CSRF protection (`skip_before_action :verify_authenticity_token` is forbidden)
- Do not disable mass assignment protection; always use strong parameters via `params.expect()`
- Do not disable or weaken content security policy settings in `config/initializers/content_security_policy.rb`
